00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:47,900
The Hubble Telescope, some 20 years ago, decided to point its telescope at the darkest spot in the night sky,

151
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:54,940
and its field of view was, and if you can see that little red circle, a circle the size of a dime,

152
00:09:54,940 --> 00:10:01,260
held a football field away, and all you see pointed at the darkest spot in the night sky,

153
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:07,860
and all you see is through that one little hole, and here's the picture that they came up with.

154
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:13,840
And the amazing thing is, that those aren't stars, those four are galaxies.

155
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:21,580
I mean, our universe is unbelievably expansive.

156
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:26,520
God is unbelievably creative.

157
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:32,340
Someone estimated that there were this number, stars, and the number doesn't even sit on the slide.

